- data/repo/SavedViewRepositoryContractTest.kt    (MockEngine: endpoint/method/params/body + per-route evict)

=== PARITY ===
Reads / queries (1 — the web file's single useQuery, listed by the prompt under "mutations"):
- useSavedViews(route)                  -> SavedViewsStore.savedViews(route): StateFlow<Resource<List<SavedView>>>
    GET /saved-views?route=<route>  (savedViewListQuery: always sends route)
    cache key = route (web savedViewsKeys.list(route)); staleTime STANDARD 60s -> CacheDomain.SavedViews 1m
    always-an-array guarantee preserved; no select/derivation (web applies none); SI verbatim

Mutations / actions (4):
- useCreateSavedView                    -> SavedViewsStore.createSavedView(input)
    POST /saved-views  body{name,route,query,[is_default],[is_pinned],[sort_order]} (optionals omitted when null)
    invalidate savedViewsKeys.list(created.route): repo evicts created.route key; store refreshes created.route feed
- useUpdateSavedView                    -> SavedViewsStore.updateSavedView(UpdateSavedViewArgs{id,route,patch})
    PUT /saved-views/{id}  body=JSON.stringify(patch) (only changed fields; id path-only)
    invalidate savedViewsKeys.list(vars.route): repo evicts route key; store refreshes route feed
- useDeleteSavedView                    -> SavedViewsStore.deleteSavedView(DeleteSavedViewArgs{id,route})
    DELETE /saved-views/{id}  (204 No Content; empty body read-as-text + discarded)
    invalidate savedViewsKeys.list(route): repo evicts route key; store refreshes route feed
    [web uses optimistic remove+broadcast; the cache-then-network analogue is evict(route)+refresh(route)]
- useSetDefaultSavedView                -> SavedViewsStore.setDefaultSavedView(SetDefaultSavedViewArgs{id,route,isDefault})
    PUT /saved-views/{id}  body={is_default}  (same endpoint as Update, body is ONLY is_default)
    invalidate savedViewsKeys.list(vars.route): repo evicts route key; store refreshes route feed

5/5 hooks ported. SI preserved (no unit-bearing fields; query is an opaque querystring blob,
round-tripped verbatim). Display conversion is the S5 render boundary's job — not this layer.
Failed mutation refreshes nothing (web onError skips invalidation) — verified by tests.
Toasts (useMutationToast) and queryBroadcast cross-tab fanout are render/runtime concerns, not
reproduced in the UI-free core (documented deviation, not silent).

Golden vectors: NONE required — the web hook applies no select/derivation/client-side transform,
so there is no non-trivial derivation for KMP+C# to drift on. Parity is locked instead by the
shared repository contract test (endpoints/params/bodies/keys) that also pins the future C# port.

